;; parinfer-regime divergence manifest (issue 43 §5)
;;
;; cljform's parinfer regime is reindent-only; byte-equality with
;; parinfer-rust paren mode is the bar. Every INTENTIONAL deviation is
;; enumerated here with its reason; the regression test compares those
;; files against the committed `snapshots/parinfer-ours/` goldens
;; instead of the raw parinfer snapshot. If an entry ever stops matching
;; its golden, that is a regression, not a new divergence.
;;
;; An empty manifest would mean cljform's parinfer regime is
;; byte-identical to parinfer-rust on the whole corpus; it is not, for
;; the one documented reason below (vacated-line removal, SPEC §10.5 /
;; issue 14). CRLF canonicality (issue 18) is NOT a divergence against
;; the pinned parinfer-rust build (commit 1a0647d preserves the input's
;; line-separator style, matching cljform) — verified at snapshot
;; generation (manifest date).
{:divergences
 [{:file "block-inner-basic.clj"
   :reason "vacated-line removal (SPEC §10.5, issue 14): `(def x 1\n  )`
            pulls the closer up and cljform deletes the vacated line
            where parinfer-rust leaves it whitespace-only."}
  {:file "whitespace-passes.clj"
   :reason "vacated-line removal (SPEC §10.5, issue 14): `(def z\n   4\n)`
            vacates the closer's line; cljform deletes it, parinfer-rust
            leaves a blank line."}]
 :known-cljfmt-divergences
 [{:shape "a form's element whose immediately preceding element is an
            #_ (uneval) form, starting its own line, in an unindented
            list"
   :minimal-repro "(foo\n x\n (= a b)\n (conj :x)\n #_#_(= c d)\n (conj :y))\n"
   :upstream "cljfmt 0.16.6 indents the element at margin(#_-form)+2"
   :cljform "cljform indents it by the list-indent rule (second-element
            margin)"
   :status "recorded edge-case decision; such shapes are excluded from the
            differential corpus (bench files containing them are listed
            in the report, not in the committed corpus)"
   :affected-bench-files #{"analysis/java.clj" "impl/analyzer.clj"}
   :note "revisit if cljfmt upstream changes; repro via the probe
          harness in the report"}]}
